{"id": "EUVD-2026-58993", "enisaUuid": "6563d06d-24b1-3232-a882-434852eed2e2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: sch_taprio: Replace direct dequeue call with peek and qdisc_dequeue_peeked\n\nWhen taprio's software path peeks a non-work-conserving child qdisc, the\nchild stashes the peeked skb in its gso_skb; taprio_dequeue_from_txq()\nthen takes the packet with a direct child ->dequeue() call, which ignores\nthat stash, orphans the peeked skb and desyncs the child's qlen/backlog.\nWith a qfq child this re-enters the child on an emptied list and\ndereferences NULL, panicking the kernel from softirq on ordinary egress.\n\nTake the packet through qdisc_dequeue_peeked(), as sch_red and sch_sfb\nnow do. The helper returns the child's stashed skb first and is a no-op\nwhen there is none, so a work-conserving child is unaffected and the\ngated path now consumes the skb whose length was charged to the budget.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:51:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:23", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51f8af240aed903e988755af33d7491030b50ae9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17ab5f76f3899f67e5569722f334591f4b88b17b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f60d5c12e0551012cee5c272b0bcbcc78f7bb506", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ee5a7665a9080bcb05d703bf981a579436fd05e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/18d580cb00c55805633bae45e90cf22ed6b8e424", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2b7ee61989f2d39df6c2cc06f9db1aea69bdb09", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2dcebbd1ad2e180fe7b98bf346ced69a872e11e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e056e1dfcddca877dd46d704e8ec9860cfc9ec44"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cjrv-4qm5-hp28", "CVE-2026-72035"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.59, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0275dbac-3c46-3e79-8551-20a3254b21ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "036af097-ca92-33b7-ad47-c0a2e90444d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.217"}, {"id": "06a0244d-9ab2-3089-b824-661117a2489e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "122aee3e-5124-3b12-96a8-f5ee588b56ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "14094261-109e-3e72-a041-4547bd3b4676", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a781ccbd19e4664babcbe4b4ead7aa2b9283d22 <18d580cb00c55805633bae45e90cf22ed6b8e424"}, {"id": "179377eb-f25d-3a89-bdb6-af2370a16356", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "26f3070e-8e25-3135-a003-6258ad1afaae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a781ccbd19e4664babcbe4b4ead7aa2b9283d22 <17ab5f76f3899f67e5569722f334591f4b88b17b"}, {"id": "2da4afe5-4197-3998-bc41-9fc52cfc05fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a781ccbd19e4664babcbe4b4ead7aa2b9283d22 <f60d5c12e0551012cee5c272b0bcbcc78f7bb506"}, {"id": "809b9daf-5f94-3a22-b5c8-bf37f6168fed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8d950d6a-57bb-3692-9b82-bb58785afcf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a781ccbd19e4664babcbe4b4ead7aa2b9283d22 <e2b7ee61989f2d39df6c2cc06f9db1aea69bdb09"}, {"id": "9063c77a-f8d6-3bb2-b6f5-22216dc4e755", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a781ccbd19e4664babcbe4b4ead7aa2b9283d22 <e056e1dfcddca877dd46d704e8ec9860cfc9ec44"}, {"id": "90db5190-e8cd-3b2e-a26d-9fedff78ceed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.184"}, {"id": "b9c82d18-dae1-3c94-9f84-f5c39495